  "notes": {
    "c0001.md": "# Denise Okoro / Calder & Wills LLP\n\nGreat client, fixed process. Their AP runs invoices through a monthly approval\ncycle no amount of following up moves. Two data points so far: fifty days on\nthe last big invoice, seven on the deposit (that one got hand-approved by\nDenise directly). Budget on the fifty.\n\n- Never call this a collections problem. They pay in full, every time.\n- The real risk is ours: every vendor for their events gets a deposit within\n  days of booking, months before their balance clears.\n- Do not schedule another large event's vendor deposits to land in the same\n  week as this one's balance is still outstanding.\n",
    "p0001.md": "# Calder & Wills LLP - Winter Gala\n\nAmber, not because anything is wrong with the client - because of timing.\nVenue, catering, florals and AV deposits are all already paid, five figures\nout the door between eighty-five and twenty days ago, plus the venue balance\npaid this week. The client's own balance invoice, 26,950, is not expected to\nclear for another six or seven weeks given their history.\n\nThat gap is why cash is thin right now, not any one bad decision. Watch\n`os cash 90` on this one, not `os aging` - aging will just say Calder is fine,\nwhich is true and beside the point.\n"
  }
